{# ── the section heading inside the rail ─────────────────────────────────────
   `text-ink-400`, not `ink-500`: on the `ink-900` rail, ink-500 is 4.0:1 — just
   under AA for 11px text. ink-400 clears it at ~6.5:1 and is still visibly quieter
   than the items it groups, which is the whole job of a heading.

   `first:pt-0` because when a role's menu opens with a heading (landlord, agent),
   the heading is the first child and its top padding would push the whole rail down
   by 20px for no reason.

   `x-show="!q.trim()"` — while the filter is in use the headings get out of the
   way. Once the list is narrowed to two or three rows, a group label above them is
   noise, not structure.

   `-mx-3 px-6` makes the heading's background span the scroll container so items
   passing under it are hidden; `px-6` keeps its text on the same 24px line as the
   items below it (nav padding 12 + item padding 12). #}
{% macro section(label) %}
    <p x-show="!q.trim()"
       class="sticky top-16 z-10 -mx-3 bg-black/25 px-6 pb-1.5 pt-5 text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.08em] text-ink-300 backdrop-blur-md">{{ label }}</p>
{% endmacro %}

{# ── one row of the rail ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   HEIGHT IS 44px IN THE DRAWER, 40px IN THE RAIL.
   44 below md because there the rail *is* the drawer and it is operated with a
   thumb (MOBILE-FIRST prime directive). 40 from md up because a persistent desktop
   rail is scanned with an eye, not tapped — and this menu runs to 40 items, where
   44px rows add up to 1,760px of scrolling.

   ACTIVE STATE: `bg-accent-600 text-white`, i.e. the one token the design system
   reserves for *interactive*. It replaced three different ad-hoc highlights —
   `bg-gray-800`, `bg-indigo-900`, `bg-blue-900` — used across three menus for the
   same concept. `aria-current="page"` goes on with it, because a colour is not a
   state as far as a screen reader is concerned. #}
{% macro item(href, icon, label, active = false) %}
    <a href="{{ href }}"{% if active %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}
       data-label="{{ label|lower }}"
       x-show="matches($el.dataset.label)"
       class="flex min-h-[44px] items-center gap-3 rounded-lg px-3 text-sm transition-colors focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-inset focus-visible:ring-accent-400 md:min-h-[40px] {{- active
            ? ' bg-accent-600 font-semibold text-white'
            : ' font-medium text-ink-300 hover:bg-white/10 hover:text-white' }}">
        {{ _self.icon(icon) }}
        <span class="truncate">{{ label }}</span>
    </a>
{% endmacro %}
